    {
      "id": 1,
      "start": 0.35,
      "end": 3.881,
      "text": "Sunlight looks white, but it carries every colour of the rainbow."
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "start": 4.181,
      "end": 9.567,
      "text": "When it hits the air, tiny molecules scatter short blue wavelengths far more than red ones."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "start": 9.867,
      "end": 14.817,
      "text": "That scattered blue reaches your eyes from every direction, so the whole sky glows blue."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "start": 15.117,
      "end": 20.98,
      "text": "At sunset, light crosses much more air, the blue is scattered away, and reds and oranges are left."
    }
  ],
